#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124227 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124498 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f232aed9-1584-5e57-a881-226a6876384a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/id #uuid "001af492-25b1-5f75-b030-668708eee118" :question/math-academy-id "e-15602" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations: \n![](images/a6/a664a3af1ba466491d209dadd32a3be026a5179ac2d0281b55f30917f9ab016b.png)\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?" :question/worked-solution "These parametric equations are equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2+2t \\\\ 5t \\\\ 1-t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2t \\\\ 5t \\\\ -t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124228 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124499 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3699391-68e8-5c59-8ca2-83fded9f22de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Parallel To a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/id #uuid "7a6038c2-3f7b-5dfa-a9e2-256b246fcc20" :question/math-academy-id "e-15603" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n![](images/f1/f161e07945eb3fe2350a56ab5cb96fa0ae2d055eb3b4cc633abfae30839ec76f.png)\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5-t \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-t \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nThis implies that the line passes through the point $(5,3,1)$ and is parallel to the vector ![](images/11/11701a2d63851a3f241d8bd905693abaaa6eda6fe4ba0c5710c92d8189595ffd.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124229 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124500 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "debd4ccc-de40-55a6-9236-9bf9fff0bdb1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Line"}] :question/id #uuid "173b99e8-d00c-57c8-995e-ba198361480e" :question/math-academy-id "e-15604" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the line shown in the figure below.\n\n![](images/53/53386f04f4025fda6ab579113a8ecb53a19f4dc0a77903adc05bac3a71429717.png)" :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(3,3,-5)$ and $Q(1,0,-1)$. Now, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2t \\\\ -3t \\\\ 4t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3-2t \\\\ 3-3t \\\\ -5+4t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-2t \\\\ y=3-3t \\\\ z=-5+4t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124230 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124501 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d275a218-aa12-54bd-a4ff-4be892226f4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Segment"}] :question/id #uuid "a9c13555-9d30-5dfc-be5a-13f0597c2ada" :question/math-academy-id "e-15605" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overline{PQ},$ where $P(1,-5,3)$ and $Q(0, 4, -4).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-t \\\\ 9t \\\\ -7t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1-t \\\\ -5+9t \\\\ 3-7t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t \\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overline{PQ}$ are the following:\n![](images/c3/c3747cbb9a88a419d6808959c490089c79041cc8773651fac1953f4846839c14.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262683 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124498 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f232aed9-1584-5e57-a881-226a6876384a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b3ac191-12b6-5c33-91e8-bbd4a678d9f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260110} {:answer/id #uuid "719300ed-b66d-5ef7-948a-e789424c8860" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260870} {:answer/id #uuid "d9c205ed-4649-5f19-88f8-87916ee72aa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261797} {:answer/id #uuid "f11d4c74-d625-59aa-b523-1bbeb463a6d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261988} {:answer/id #uuid "f7c34baa-0ca8-5341-8f9f-6f7d7be8ac04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262042}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f11d4c74-d625-59aa-b523-1bbeb463a6d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261988} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa8a3fcc-2ead-55f3-87b6-42aa969a4b28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262428}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "66b1db3e-6731-578f-a2e5-78774370e2fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-126997" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-3 \\\\ y=5t \\\\ z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?" :question/worked-solution "These parametric equations are equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5t \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124779 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124499 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3699391-68e8-5c59-8ca2-83fded9f22de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Parallel To a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86184092-f8ab-5f5d-b96f-e4866caec311" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -7 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121272} {:answer/id #uuid "93ce67a9-85f7-5c77-9689-e8415c8d8352" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121273} {:answer/id #uuid "bd84e67f-f595-5bf0-a553-0c0c9124aacd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121274} {:answer/id #uuid "097179f2-ee70-56c0-9915-72fb57f9f470" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ -7 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121275} {:answer/id #uuid "60501393-bbb6-5456-8be6-a929d27f080a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{4}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121276}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8dcca8ea-5fb3-5b9a-99d6-1597b6b765e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121271}] :question/id #uuid "6ab6a329-d125-54e3-98aa-c411b7b2d383" :question/math-academy-id "q-127045" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n${x = 3t - 12; y =-5 - 7t; z = \\frac{3}{4}t + \\frac{1}{5}$\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262704 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124500 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "debd4ccc-de40-55a6-9236-9bf9fff0bdb1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06f568ab-a709-5bca-88dc-51b139dea190" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=7-3t \\\\ y=-11-2t \\\\ z=4+7t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259941} {:answer/id #uuid "2d9646e2-26ba-5539-b5b9-a9f710e6f312" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=7+3t \\\\ y=-11+2t \\\\ z=3-7t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260284} {:answer/id #uuid "a893ca4e-abe1-5c54-8923-2af72867921f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=7+3t \\\\ y=11+2t \\\\ z=3-7t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261346} {:answer/id #uuid "c3323d37-5851-523c-9118-ccd184deb6cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=7+3t \\\\ y=11-2t \\\\ z=3+7t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261598} {:answer/id #uuid "e1f2d66d-9fc7-5bf5-b020-43c58962e2ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=7-3t \\\\ y=-11+2t \\\\ z=3+7t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1f2d66d-9fc7-5bf5-b020-43c58962e2ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=7-3t \\\\ y=-11+2t \\\\ z=3+7t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261866} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c40d077-b693-5acd-b033-066f298637d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262258}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b0a75f14-5c7e-5e9b-9922-914a01571a2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-127065" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the straight line that passes through $P(7,-11,3)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨-3,2,7⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, the vector equation of the line is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3t \\\\ 2t \\\\ 7t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7-3t \\\\ -11+2t \\\\ 3+7t\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Therefore, the parametric equations are:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=7-3t \\\\ y=-11+2t \\\\ z=3+7t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290404 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124500 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "debd4ccc-de40-55a6-9236-9bf9fff0bdb1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a5a3afe-de20-5eff-8acd-278f99180d3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=3-t \\\\ y=-2+t \\\\ z=2+4t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288546} {:answer/id #uuid "62953b2c-180e-5684-8312-080f1a4c3859" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=4t \\\\ y=-3t \\\\ z=-2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288721} {:answer/id #uuid "6a54827d-c7ce-534b-9371-072edb5b00b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+4t \\\\ y=1-3t \\\\ z=4-2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288784} {:answer/id #uuid "c094fd28-4889-5b9c-b86c-cf25683234de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=4-t \\\\ y=-3+t \\\\ z=-2+4t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289307} {:answer/id #uuid "f6dedf7b-91ad-53cb-9328-647bbe4eb870" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-t \\\\ y=t \\\\ z=4t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a54827d-c7ce-534b-9371-072edb5b00b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+4t \\\\ y=1-3t \\\\ z=4-2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288784} :answer-field/id #uuid "80150ea8-e109-5771-a019-7ef7f30cdd17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290010}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "903d4e8d-5aeb-56dc-9b7a-c2b3d8e18a20" :question/math-academy-id "q-22318" :question/problem "![](images/58/58076d96d149ff4521103fd15c7187bc1a58595ab20f28be92be0f79385aee61.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the line shown in the figure above." :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(-1,1,4)$ and $Q(3,-2,2).$ Now, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$,  as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4t \\\\ -3t \\\\ -2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1+4t \\\\ 1-3t \\\\ 4-2t\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Therefore, the parametric equations are:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+4t \\\\ y=1-3t \\\\ z=4-2t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124846 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124501 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d275a218-aa12-54bd-a4ff-4be892226f4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a1ed3b7-02bb-5f9d-9c31-7eddaa80fb8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2+3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a1ed3b7-02bb-5f9d-9c31-7eddaa80fb8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2+3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288545} :answer-field/id #uuid "35127a82-230c-5025-ac87-eb4dafe53c72" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2292b4c-0ec4-5867-a7de-bf2a67a209e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2292b4c-0ec4-5867-a7de-bf2a67a209e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289115} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cd8b28a-ec40-5b78-9910-db2d429ee40b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289969} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee2a1d96-a32c-5a2f-8cd6-6537695d26a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee2a1d96-a32c-5a2f-8cd6-6537695d26a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289601} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8e6d5ec-636b-572a-8af3-3a4e8d1a2fd5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290135}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9a10a92-511c-5609-8370-301fff1b284f" :question/math-academy-id "q-236389" :question/problem "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(1,4,-2)$ and $Q(-2,3,1).$\n\n| $x=$ | {{field-1}} | $t\\in [0,$ {{field-2}} $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y=$ | $4-t$ |  |\n| $z=$ | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3t \\\\ -t \\\\ 3t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1-3t \\\\ 4-t \\\\ -2+3t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t\\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1-3t \\\\ y=4-t \\\\ z=-2+3t\\end{aligned}\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290483 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124501 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d275a218-aa12-54bd-a4ff-4be892226f4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0d37c05-2222-5148-9aec-f93cfef96b82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+8t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0d37c05-2222-5148-9aec-f93cfef96b82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+8t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289105} :answer-field/id #uuid "3edaf7a3-5c39-5fa1-b351-32d25769c0fd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289869} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72e40c90-b0e3-54bc-9132-cdc3a3ae116d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72e40c90-b0e3-54bc-9132-cdc3a3ae116d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288832} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c6dcef5-21d8-5104-bb44-42638c6a463d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d2d5d8fc-9cc6-565a-9a90-d1ac2885d17a" :question/math-academy-id "q-236988" :question/problem "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(6,2,1)$ and $Q(4,10,2).$\n\n| $x=$ | $6-2t$ | $t\\in [0,$ {{field-1}} $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y=$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| $z=$ | $1+t$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2t \\\\ 8t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6-2t \\\\ 2+8t \\\\ 1+t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t\\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=6-2t \\\\ y=2+8t \\\\ z=1+t\\end{aligned}\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124949 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124498 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f232aed9-1584-5e57-a881-226a6876384a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd44e118-b9d7-5b0d-aa4b-86097c349fbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = t\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}, 